[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm coming from Rocq and experimenting with LEAN. In Rocq, we can write something like <code>Arguments foo _%_my_scope.</code> to get Rocq to automatically open the scope <code>my_scope</code> around the first argument of <code>foo</code>. In Rocq notation, this basically means that <code>foo x</code> is interpreted as <code>foo x%my_scope</code>. From what I have read, it seems like this requires defining a macro that wraps the definition in LEAN. Is that correct? Or is there a simpler way to do this?</p>",
        "id": 611259825,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784284996
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a particular reason you are looking for this feature? This is not something that people in Lean usually need to write down what they want to</p>",
        "id": 611261924,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1784285894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm very new to LEAN (I'm in the hours range), so I really am just not certain what I am doing. At the moment, I am writing some very simple definitions in LEAN Iris and I find that I have to write <code>iprop(forall x, ..)</code> everywhere instead of simply <code>forall x, ...</code>.</p>",
        "id": 611262291,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784286041
    },
    {
